{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.ConjAtomBraidExteriorAlgebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.ConjAtomBraidExteriorAlgebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Sum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":42,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium4_dominant_pair_transpose_related","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium4_dominant_pair_transpose_related","kind":"theorem","line":495,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L495-L511","doc":"**THEOREM (bar-involution alignment).** For ⁴He, the dominant\npartition (4, 4, 4) AND its transpose (3, 3, 3, 3) both appear in\nthe top-5 most-negative min_eig list. This is the Wedderburn-level\nmanifestation of the bar-involution Δ_λ = Δ_{λ^T} structure\n(AGENTS.md §7b Type-B folding).\n\nThe structural meaning: the bar-anti-symmetric content of the\ncanonical atom-braid σ_avg crossings populates **transpose-paired**\nirreps. Per the analysis, both partitions have min_eig in [−19.84,\n−15.5] — they are simultaneously the most-non-PSD blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_3_2_2_2_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_3_2_2_2_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":492,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L492-L493","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_4_4_4_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_4_4_4_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":487,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L487-L490","doc":"**THEOREM.** Transposition is an involution (λ^TT = λ) — the\ncategorical bar-involution at the Wedderburn level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_3_1_1_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_3_1_1_1","kind":"theorem","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L482-L485","doc":"**THEOREM.** Transpose of the deuteron dominant (3, 1, 1, 1) is\na 3-cell hook. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_3_2_2_2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_3_2_2_2","kind":"theorem","line":475,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L475-L480","doc":"**THEOREM.** Transpose of (3, 2, 2, 2) — the dominant partition for\nBOTH T and ³He (which share n_0 = 9). Conjugate is (4, 4, 1) — a\ndifferent shape, but symmetric in a structural sense (almost-square\nminus a corner). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_4_4_4_eq_3_3_3_3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugate_4_4_4_eq_3_3_3_3","kind":"theorem","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L468-L473","doc":"**THEOREM (verification).** Transpose of (4, 4, 4) is (3, 3, 3, 3).\nBoth partitions are in the top-5 most-negative min_eig for ⁴He's\ncanonical atom-braid (see `alpha-star-dominant-partitions.witness.json`).\nThis is the bar-involution structure in the α* analysis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugatePartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.conjugatePartition","kind":"def","line":457,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L457-L466","doc":"Conjugate (transpose) of a partition. Standard Young-diagram\ntranspose: for λ = (λ_1, ..., λ_k), the conjugate λ^T has\nλ^T_i = |{j : λ_j ≥ i}|. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium4_lp_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium4_lp_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":434,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L434-L443","doc":"**Quantitative reduction for ⁴He:** 77 partition channels → ≤ 11\nactive. The conjecture says the LP/SDP feasibility region shrinks\nfrom 77-dim (Wedderburn) to ≤ 11-dim (categorically active) — a\n≥ 7× constraint tightening that resolves the prior under-determination. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.lp_channel_reduction_verified","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.lp_channel_reduction_verified","kind":"theorem","line":418,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L418-L432","doc":"**THEOREM (LP-channel reduction for D, T, ³He, ⁴He).** The conjectured\nactive-channel count is strictly less than the full partition count\np(3A) for each of the 4 empirically-verified atoms — a categorical\nunder-determination fix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.partition_number_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.partition_number_small","kind":"def","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L400-L416","doc":"p(n) — the partition number of n.\nHardcoded for small n via the OEIS A000041 sequence (decidable). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.max_active_channels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.max_active_channels","kind":"def","line":396,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L396-L398","doc":"Predicted maximum active LP-channel count under the conjecture:\nn* + 1 = (3A − Z) + 1, one per non-zero grade of Λ*(R^(3A−Z)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.atom_braid_exterior_algebra_via_step4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.atom_braid_exterior_algebra_via_step4","kind":"theorem","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L370-L384","doc":"**Atom-braid conjecture, factored through Step 4.**\n\nRecords the Pascal-sum identity together with the Step 4\nobligation in a single statement: once Step 4 is discharged\n(i.e., once a proof of `AvgCrossingPreservesGradeHolds Z N`\nis provided as the class field), both the dimensional shape\nAND its structural meaning are delivered. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.step4_implies_exterior_algebra_structure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.step4_implies_exterior_algebra_structure","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L336-L368","doc":"**Step 4-augmented structural result.** Given the Step 4\nhypothesis for `(Z, N)`, both\n(a) the `AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure` instance, and\n(b) the witness of `AvgCrossingPreservesGradeHolds Z N`,\nare available together.\n\nHonest scope: (a) is currently derivable from `Z_pos` alone —\n`AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure`'s structural-shape fields\n(`n₀`, `n_star`, `delta`, `total_dim`, `shape`) are all\ndefaulted formulas, so they require no Steps 1-3 obligation\nat the field level. The dimension-shape FACTS for individual\natoms are proved by `decide` in this file.  The *structural\nreason* — that this shape is in fact what the canonical\natom-braid produces — is precisely the\n`AvgCrossingPreservesGradeHolds` content carried in (b).\n\nMathematical reading: until `AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure`\ngains a proof-bearing field connecting its dimension formula to\nthe canonical Hecke sub-algebra, the Step 4 content lives in\n`AvgCrossingPreservesGradeHolds`, not in the structural class.\nDischarging Step 4 is therefore: instance\n`AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis` → supply a proof of\n`AvgCrossingPreservesGradeHolds Z N` → both (a) and (b)\navailable together. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis.avg_crossing_preserves_grade","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis.avg_crossing_preserves_grade","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L334-L334","doc":"Proof of the specific Step 4 obligation — that inter-nucleon\nAvg crossings preserve the Boolean grading of the canonical\natom-braid's Coxeter-length filtration.  Typed by the named\n`AvgCrossingPreservesGradeHolds Z N` opaque Prop above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis.Z_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis.Z_pos","kind":"theorem","line":329,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L329-L329","doc":"Positive proton count (consistent with\n`AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L326-L326","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis","kind":"class","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L318-L334","doc":"**PR-D Step 4 hypothesis** — the inter-nucleon Avg-crossing\nBoolean-grading preservation claim, axiomatised as a class\nfield per AGENTS.md §3b-cond.\n\nThe field `avg_crossing_preserves_grade` carries a proof of\nthe *specific* named Prop `AvgCrossingPreservesGradeHolds Z N`,\nnot an arbitrary `Prop` — so any instance is forced to\ndischarge the actual Step 4 obligation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AvgCrossingPreservesGradeHolds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AvgCrossingPreservesGradeHolds","kind":"opaque","line":294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L294-L316","doc":"**The Step 4 categorical claim, as a named opaque Prop.**\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond + the audit\n`docs/audits/2026-05-30-atom-braid-categorical-proof-feasibility.md`'s\nfailure-mode #4 (\"axiomatising more just relocates the sorry\"),\nStep 4 must be a *specific* Prop, not a `Prop`-typed slot, so\nany `AtomBraidStep4Hypothesis` instance is forced to discharge\na named obligation rather than supply an arbitrary proposition.\n\nInformally: for the canonical atom-braid\n`T_w(Z, N) ∈ H_{3A}(q)`, every inter-nucleon Avg crossing\n`σ_{3k+2} − h/2` acts by left/right-multiplication on the\nCoxeter-length filtration preserving the Boolean grading — i.e.\nit maps `F_k → F_k` without expanding the binary-DOF count\n`n* = 3A − Z`.\n\nFormally we leave this `opaque` until the\n`coxeterLengthFiltration` API in `QOU.IwahoriHecke.*` is\nexposed (Sprint 5 follow-up). At that point this declaration\nwill be promoted from `opaque` to a concrete `def` over the\nfiltration accessor; any existing instances become real\nproofs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.atom_braid_exterior_algebra_structure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.atom_braid_exterior_algebra_structure","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L242-L262","doc":"**THEOREM SKETCH (general conjecture, proof deferred).**\nFor all `Z ≥ 1, N ≥ 0`, the GB-NF filtration of\n`T_w(Z, N) = atom_braid_word_3A(Z, N)` in `H_{3A}(q)` has\ndimension `2^(3A − Z)`, with Pascal-row structure\n`dim(F_k) = C(3A−Z, k−(Z−1))`.\n\nStatus: the 5-step structural argument is documented above;\nfull Lean discharge is the natural follow-up. The 4 verified\natom cases (`deuteron/tritium/helium3/helium4_pascal_row` +\n`*_total_dim_eq_*`) are proved by `decide`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium3_pascal_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium3_pascal_row","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L186-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.tritium_pascal_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.tritium_pascal_row","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L180-L184","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.deuteron_pascal_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.deuteron_pascal_row","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L170-L178","doc":"**Pascal-row checks for the 3 lighter verified atoms** (D, T, ³He).\nEach is the observed filtration shape from the Rust solver\n(`joint-tower-sdp-rust.witness.json`) matched against the predicted\nbinomial coefficients. All discharged by `decide` on the binomial\nidentity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium4_pascal_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium4_pascal_row","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L160-L168","doc":"**Structural shape check for ⁴He:** the filtration values\n{1, 10, 45, 120, 210, 252, 210, 120, 45, 10, 1} match Pascal's\ntriangle row 10 — verified by direct `decide` on the binomial\ncoefficient identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.verified_atoms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.verified_atoms","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L153-L158","doc":"**THEOREM (verified-cases enumeration).** The conjecture has been\nempirically verified by direct GB-NF reduction in the Rust solver\nfor D, T, ³He, ⁴He. This theorem records the verified-atom list. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.filtration_shape_sum_eq_total_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.filtration_shape_sum_eq_total_dim","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L136-L151","doc":"**THEOREM (combinatorial closure).** For any atom (Z, N) with Z ≥ 1,\nthe sum of the filtration-shape values over k ∈ [δ, δ + n*] equals\nthe total dimension 2^(3A − Z).\n\nThis is the closure check: the conjectured filtration-shape\ndistribution is internally consistent — its grade-wise sum matches\nthe total dim claimed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.binomial_sum_pow_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.binomial_sum_pow_two","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L130-L134","doc":"**Combinatorial identity (verifies Pascal's binomial sum at each n*).**\nThe sum of binomial coefficients over a row equals 2^n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.boron11_total_dim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.boron11_total_dim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L122-L128","doc":"**Verification for ¹¹B (Z=5, N=6):** total dim 2²⁸ = 268435456.\nFirst A=11 (boron-11) atom-braid in `H_{33}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.beryllium9_total_dim_eq_8388608","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.beryllium9_total_dim_eq_8388608","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L113-L120","doc":"**Verification for ⁹Be (Z=4, N=5):** total dim 2²³ = 8388608.\nFirst A=9 (beryllium-9) atom-braid in `H_{27}(q)`. Predicted\nexterior-algebra dimension `2^(3·9 - 4) = 2^23 = 8388608`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.lithium6_total_dim_eq_32768","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.lithium6_total_dim_eq_32768","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L102-L111","doc":"**Verification for ⁶Li (Z=3, N=3):** total dim 2¹⁵ = 32768.\nSprint follow-up: extends the verified-atom set from 4 (D, T, ³He, ⁴He)\nto 5 with the first A=6 nucleus. The lithium-6 atom-braid lives in\n`H_{18}(q)`; the predicted exterior-algebra dimension is `2^(3·6 - 3)\n= 2^15 = 32768`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium4_total_dim_eq_1024","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium4_total_dim_eq_1024","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L95-L100","doc":"**Verification for ⁴He (Z=2, N=2):** total dim 2¹⁰ = 1024. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium3_total_dim_eq_128","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.helium3_total_dim_eq_128","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L88-L93","doc":"**Verification for ³He (Z=2, N=1):** total dim 2⁷ = 128. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.tritium_total_dim_eq_256","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.tritium_total_dim_eq_256","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L81-L86","doc":"**Verification for tritium ³H (Z=1, N=2):** total dim 2⁸ = 256. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.deuteron_total_dim_eq_32","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.deuteron_total_dim_eq_32","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L74-L79","doc":"**Verification for deuteron ²H (Z=1, N=1):** total dim 2⁵ = 32. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.shape","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L72-L72","doc":"Filtration shape: dim(F_k) = C(n*, k − δ) for k ∈ [δ, δ + n*]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.total_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.total_dim","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Total dimension of the sub-algebra: 2^(3A − Z). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.delta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.delta","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Grade shift δ = Z − 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.n_star","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.n_star","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Number of binary degrees of freedom n* = 3A − Z. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.n₀_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.n₀_eq","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L64-L64","doc":"n₀ is exactly 3(Z + N). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.n₀","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.n₀","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L62-L62","doc":"Atomic strand count n₀ = 3A = 3(Z + N). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.Z_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.Z_pos","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Positive proton count (every atom has at least 1 proton in\nthe QOU convention; quark-only sectors are out of scope). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure.mk","kind":"ctor","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebra.AtomBraidExteriorAlgebraStructure","kind":"class","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.lean#L43-L72","doc":"Conjectural class encoding the filtration-shape structure of\nthe canonical atom-braid `T_w(Z, N)` in `H_{3A}(q)`.\n\nThe structural claim: the GB-NF filtration on the sub-algebra\ngenerated by `T_w(Z, N)` has shape\n\n  dim(F_k) = C(3A − Z, k − (Z − 1))\n\nfor k in [Z − 1, 3A − 1], with total dim 2^(3A − Z).\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond, this is the sole `sorry`-equivalent\ninput for downstream propositions; the empirical verification\nis recorded in `joint-tower-sdp-rust.witness.json` for D, T,\n³He, ⁴He. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:atom-braid-exterior-algebra","label":"conj:atom-braid-exterior-algebra","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/conj-atom-braid-exterior-algebra.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}